From bd99a8b84cc62fb1d9527a5ff271bf29875e2ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:05:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] camera: the fps ceiling is the lower of Core's table and
 the probe again

Why: The port made the startup probe the whole fps ceiling for a sensor
mode and kept the old rule behind APERTAR_FPS_LIMIT=table. 1.6.0 had the
table alone (CameraController.cpp:2669-2671@upstream-1.6.0) and fork main
lets the probe only lower it: min(table, probe)
(CameraController.cpp:2763-2769@f60e301). With the port's default a stock
camera offers 60 fps at 4K 12-bit where 1.6.0 offered 30. The owner's rig
needs the probe alone, so that becomes the switch and the 1.6.0 value the
default. The port also left dead code around the ceiling: backendMaximumFps
always returned nothing and three wrappers called it, and
APERTAR_IMX283_PROBE_FPS was a second knob for one sensor.

What: maximumSupportedFpsForResolution returns the table when the probe
has no value, else min(table, probe). APERTAR_FPS_LIMIT=probe, read at
use, returns the probe alone; unset or "table" means the default. The
IMX283 keeps min(probe, its crop_vmax=0 floor) under every value, because
its probe can report more than the sensor delivers. The effective knob is
echoed as fps_limit=probe on the "ApertarCore recording clip:" line.
Deleted: fpsLimitTableOnly, imx283ProbeFpsOnly and
APERTAR_IMX283_PROBE_FPS, backendMaximumFps and its three wrappers,
resolveSensorMaxFps and applyBackendCap in FpsCeiling.hpp with their test
lines, and the comment that named the old knob. boolEnvValue moves back
inside the libcamera guard next to unsignedEnvValue, its last unguarded
user is gone. FpsCeiling.hpp keeps the lossless fps helpers.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the host tests pass with no new
warning (fps_ceiling_test lost the cases of the deleted functions). In
--simulate the sensor is Unknown and there is no probe, so the changed
rule is not reached there; no reply field changed. Needs the camera, no
env knob: get_state at 3840x2160 12-bit shows fps_max 30. With
APERTAR_FPS_LIMIT=probe in the unit environment: fps_max 60, and the
take's line has fps_limit=probe
(journalctl -u apertar-core -b | grep 'recording clip:'). Deploy note:
the owner's systemd drop-in must carry APERTAR_FPS_LIMIT=probe before this reaches
his camera, because the sanitised fps is saved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
